# SEO Baseline

SEO is not a launch-only cleanup task. For every generated website, public web
app, marketing route, content route, docs surface, or public SPA shell, invoke
the `seo` skill and ship the technical SEO baseline before calling the work
complete.

For projects with no web surface, record `SEO baseline: Not applicable` in the
handoff or docs and state the reason. For private authenticated routes and admin
surfaces, apply `noindex,nofollow` while still keeping share and title metadata
correct for browser tabs and internal previews.

## Generated Web Baseline

New generated React/Vite, Ionic web, explicit Next.js, or other public web
projects must include:

- A route-aware SEO layer:
  - React/Vite or Ionic SPA: `Seo.tsx` plus `src/lib/seo.ts` or the local
    equivalent. It updates `document.title`, description, robots, canonical,
    Open Graph, Twitter Card, and JSON-LD per route.
  - Next.js or another metadata-aware framework: use the framework-native
    metadata API, but still satisfy the same fields and structured-data rules.
- Route metadata for every public route: unique title, description, canonical
  URL, robots value, Open Graph/Twitter image, and JSON-LD for the primary
  entity visible on that route.
- Fallback metadata in the HTML/app shell: title, description, canonical,
  `og:*`, `twitter:*`, favicon links, and manifest link.
- Public crawl/share assets: `robots.txt`, `sitemap.xml`,
  `manifest.webmanifest`, `favicon.ico`, `apple-touch-icon`, app icons
  (`192x192` and `512x512` where applicable), and a default
  `1200x630` PNG/JPG Open Graph image.
- A public site URL env var in the committed example env file:
  `VITE_SITE_URL` for Vite/Ionic or the framework's public site-url equivalent.
  Real production domains are user/host inputs; mark them `Unverified` until
  supplied and never invent a deploy URL.
- Regression coverage that proves every created or changed public route has the
  expected title, description, canonical URL, Open Graph image, JSON-LD, and
  sitemap inclusion, and that private/admin routes emit `noindex,nofollow`.
- A note in `.traffic-one/deployment.md` or `.traffic-one/known-issues.md` when an SPA route
  must rank but lacks prerendering/static rendering or equivalent host support.
  Do not claim full SEO parity for client-rendered shells alone.

## Existing Project Reconciliation

Before normal feature work in `existing-codebase` or `existing-with-supabase`
mode, inspect the current web surface:

- Locate route definitions, app shell HTML, public assets, metadata helpers,
  sitemap/robots generation, and existing SEO tests before adding anything.
- Preserve mature framework-native metadata systems; extend them instead of
  replacing them with a parallel helper.
- If the baseline is missing or partial, add the smallest compatible SEO layer
  and assets listed above.
- If the baseline exists, update route metadata, sitemap/robots, structured
  data, and tests for every changed public route.
- Never overwrite brand/domain metadata blindly; keep existing verified values
  and mark unknown production domains as `Unverified`.

## Review And Test Gate

Reviewers request changes when public web work lacks route-level title,
description, canonical, Open Graph/Twitter image, JSON-LD, sitemap/robots,
favicon/PWA basics, or SEO regression coverage for every created or changed
public route. Testers add or update Playwright/unit coverage for metadata when
routes are created or changed.
